Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-16-2000||09:30 AM||||For those of you interested in Eddy Snaauws custom dash, here's some info for you.<P>Eddy sold his dash to a gentleman in Vegas.  The current owner, Scott Tilden, has recently received the dash molds.  I spoke with him (Scott T.) the other day.  He said that he wants to take some time to "fix" some minor imperfections.  Eddy built this originally as a one off for his car only, but since Scott will be mass producing them, he wants thing slightly different. <BR>For those of you who love the design as I do, there shouldn't be any major changes in looks.  He's considering a keyed lock for the console mounted glove box as well as some minor changes to the dash mounted glove box and the way that the switches are mounted.  (Apparently the recessed configuration isn't as good as a flush mounted one?)<BR>He plans on trying some vinyl paint, too.  He thinks that it would be cost prohibitive to cover them in leather as Eddy has done on his although he doesn't think that it would be tough to do.  (Leather must be expensive.)<BR>His current thought on price is somewhere around $1400 uncovered, but complete.  He is envisioning a number of options as far as coverings.  Vinyl paint, leather, cloth?, who knows what, all with their own price adjustments.  <BR>He said it shouldn't take more than about 3 hours to install once your dash is out of the car.  This dash should be better mounted than the original, too.  He said that the only modifications you should need to make on your car is lengthening the wiring harnesses for the headlight/dimmer and trunk/defroster switches and moving them to the other side of the steering column.<BR>Scott T. promised me that he would keep me updated as to the progress and will send pics as soon as he can.<BR>I'll post what I know when I know it.<BR>Hopefully he'll be ready to market this in the next couple of months.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||10
